WEBVTT

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:07.131
Captain's Log, Stardate 49655.2.

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:09.539
Our sensors have located
a variety of flower

00:00:09.576 --> 00:00:12.704
which may prove to be a valuable
nutritional supplement.

00:00:12.746 --> 00:00:16.238
I've sent Mr. Neelix and
Mr. Tuvok to collect samples.

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:19.280
Whoa!

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:21.378
Smell that air, Mr. Vulcan!

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:24.151
Look at that sky!

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:27.159
Oh, it's an exhilarating day,
isn't it?

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:29.855
As you well know by now,
Mr. Neelix,

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:31.864
I do not experience
exhilaration.

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:35.334
Oh, let's not quibble
about semantics.

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:37.996
A breeze is blowing,
the sun is shining.

00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:39.972
It's beautiful.

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:42.998
The weather is certainly
adequate for our purposes.

00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:45.306
Adequate?

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:47.336
You know something?

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.211
You're acting

00:00:49.249 --> 00:00:51.717
more "Tuvokian"
than usual this morning.

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:53.719
I am who I am, Mr. Neelix.

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:56.221
It is impossible for me to be
more or less like myself.

00:00:56.256 --> 00:00:59.419
There you go
with the semantics again.

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:01.984
But you know
what I'm talking about.

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:04.428
I'm afraid I don't.

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:06.728
Well, then,
I'll explain it to you.

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:09.735
You're a nature lover,
aren't you?

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:11.737
I appreciate nature, yes.

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:14.638
It's one of the things that
you and I have in common.

00:01:14.674 --> 00:01:16.301
And here we are,
on a perfect day,

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:19.311
foraging for an exceptionally
lovely variety of orchid...

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:21.813
your favorite flower...
and all you can say

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:24.976
about the experience
is that it's adequate.

00:01:25.018 --> 00:01:28.146
I just... I don't see
why you're not having fun.

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:29.849
We are not here to have fun.

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:31.982
We are here to collect samples.

00:01:32.025 --> 00:01:33.720
Why?
Is there some regulation

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:36.524
that says we can't
do both at the same time?

00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:37.860
I know.

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:41.628
Why don't, why don't we sing
a song while we toil, hmm?

00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:43.363
Lt'll cheer you up.

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:44.927
I've been studying Vulcan music.

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:48.771
Uh... do you know
that lovely tune that starts:

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:52.767
O starless night

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:55.007
Of boundless black...

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:58.950
That "lovely tune"
is a traditional funeral dirge.

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:00.953
I know,

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:04.320
but it was the most cheerful
song I could find

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:05.847
in the Vulcan database.

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:08.087
Come on, Tuvok, join me.

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:10.392
O starless night

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:12.762
Of boundless black...

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:16.227
Mr. Neelix...

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:17.930
Yes?

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:19.404
Do you think
you could possibly behave

00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:21.634
a little less...
like yourself?

00:02:26.513 --> 00:02:28.174
Are Neelix and Tuvok
back from the surface?

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:30.478
Not yet. We're having some
trouble with the transporter.

00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:31.711
Captain...

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:33.878
there's a minor glitch in the
molecular imaging scanners.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:37.822
Ensign Kim should have it up
and running in a few minutes.

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:44.160
Try narrowing
the annular confinement beam.

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:47.665
How's that?

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.327
Let's try it again.

00:02:49.369 --> 00:02:50.996
Kim to away team.

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:52.629
Sorry for the delay.

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:53.696
We're ready to bring you back.

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:55.230
Acknowledged.

00:02:58.244 --> 00:02:59.905
Energize.

00:03:02.282 --> 00:03:04.443
There's something wrong, sir.

00:03:04.484 --> 00:03:06.509
I'm only getting one pattern.

00:03:06.553 --> 00:03:08.578
Tuvok or Neelix?

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:10.521
I don't think
it's either of them.

00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:12.582
Abort.

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:13.990
It's too late.

00:05:13.678 --> 00:05:14.940
Kim to Security.

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:16.447
Intruder alert,
Transporter Room 1.

00:05:16.481 --> 00:05:18.949
Identify yourself.

00:05:18.984 --> 00:05:20.713
I'm Lieutenant Tuvok.

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:25.480
And I'm Neelix.

00:05:25.523 --> 00:05:27.957
Sir, according to the
bio-scanners, he's right.

00:05:27.993 --> 00:05:30.655
Somehow their patterns
have merged.

00:05:35.567 --> 00:05:39.469
I think the logical thing
is for me to go to Sick Bay.

00:05:45.844 --> 00:05:47.402
And you recognize all of us?

00:05:47.445 --> 00:05:48.412
Of course.

00:05:48.446 --> 00:05:53.076
Doctor, Captain Janeway,
Ensign Kim...

00:05:53.118 --> 00:05:55.712
Kes.

00:05:55.754 --> 00:05:57.346
My scans indicate

00:05:57.389 --> 00:06:01.917
that all biological matter
was merged on a molecular level.

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:05.760
Proteins, enzymes,
DNA sequences.

00:06:05.797 --> 00:06:07.162
The man you see before you

00:06:07.198 --> 00:06:08.927
is literally
a fusion of two men.

00:06:09.034 --> 00:06:11.127
But he's surprisingly healthy,
considering the circumstances.

00:06:11.169 --> 00:06:12.864
All vital signs are stable.

00:06:12.904 --> 00:06:14.667
What's the last thing
you remember?

00:06:14.706 --> 00:06:20.110
I... we... that is to say,
Tuvok and Neelix,

00:06:20.145 --> 00:06:22.375
we had just finished
gathering the samples.

00:06:22.414 --> 00:06:24.814
We were beaming back
to the ship.

00:06:24.849 --> 00:06:26.214
The next thing I knew,

00:06:26.251 --> 00:06:28.549
I was standing
on the transporter pad

00:06:28.586 --> 00:06:29.712
as you see me now.

00:06:29.754 --> 00:06:33.281
I'm also picking up traces
of a third genetic pattern.

00:06:33.324 --> 00:06:34.814
It appears to be plant-based.

00:06:34.859 --> 00:06:36.759
The orchids.

00:06:36.795 --> 00:06:40.891
We had collected several dozen
samples of orchids.

00:06:40.932 --> 00:06:43.457
They were in our sample
containers when we beamed up.

00:06:43.501 --> 00:06:47.062
Well, they're part
of your genetic structure now.

00:06:47.105 --> 00:06:49.630
But they don't appear to be
affecting your biochemistry.

00:06:49.674 --> 00:06:50.936
Torres said you were
having trouble

00:06:50.975 --> 00:06:52.966
with the molecular imaging
scanners.

00:06:53.011 --> 00:06:54.069
That's right.

00:06:54.112 --> 00:06:56.080
Maybe this alien plant life

00:06:56.114 --> 00:06:58.639
affected
the scanners in some way.

00:06:58.683 --> 00:07:01.516
Possibly. I'll know more
after we've run a diagnostic

00:07:01.553 --> 00:07:03.851
on the biofilters
and transporter logs.

00:07:03.888 --> 00:07:04.912
Get on it.

00:07:07.592 --> 00:07:11.255
In the meantime, I'll send
an away team in a shuttlecraft

00:07:11.296 --> 00:07:14.925
to collect fresh samples
of the orchid for further study.

00:07:14.966 --> 00:07:18.732
Doctor, let me know as soon
as you have something more.

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:20.931
Yes, Captain.

00:07:24.709 --> 00:07:27.269
Kes, take our patient
to the Science Lab

00:07:27.312 --> 00:07:29.906
and perform a full
bio-spectral analysis.

00:07:29.948 --> 00:07:32.348
I'll start examining
the genetic data.

00:07:57.075 --> 00:07:59.908
This situation must be
very difficult for you, Kes.

00:07:59.944 --> 00:08:01.912
Perhaps it would be easier

00:08:01.946 --> 00:08:03.914
if someone else
administered these tests.

00:08:03.948 --> 00:08:08.385
Thank you for your concern,
but I'll be fine.

00:08:08.419 --> 00:08:09.613
This scan is very delicate,

00:08:09.654 --> 00:08:11.918
so try to remain still
for the next 20 minutes.

00:08:11.990 --> 00:08:13.787
I'll do my best.

00:08:13.825 --> 00:08:15.918
Don't worry.
We're going to figure it out.

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:17.928
Oh, I'm not worried.

00:08:17.962 --> 00:08:19.930
I couldn't be in better hands.

00:08:19.964 --> 00:08:22.592
This crew, you're
consummate professionals.

00:08:22.634 --> 00:08:24.124
You're my friends.

00:08:24.169 --> 00:08:26.330
My family.

00:08:26.371 --> 00:08:30.535
So worrying would be illogical,
don't you think?

00:08:30.575 --> 00:08:33.544
Would you mind if I asked you
some questions

00:08:33.578 --> 00:08:35.205
about what you're going through?

00:08:35.246 --> 00:08:36.543
Not at all.

00:08:36.581 --> 00:08:39.209
Well, do you feel
as if you're thinking

00:08:39.250 --> 00:08:40.547
with two minds...

00:08:40.585 --> 00:08:42.212
two separate minds?

00:08:42.253 --> 00:08:45.814
Are Neelix and Tuvok
inside of you, talking to me,

00:08:45.857 --> 00:08:47.848
talking to each other?

00:08:47.892 --> 00:08:50.952
If you mean am I suffering
from some form

00:08:50.995 --> 00:08:53.623
of multiple personality
disorder, I don't think so.

00:08:53.665 --> 00:08:56.634
I do have the memories
of both men,

00:08:56.668 --> 00:08:58.966
but I seem to have
a single consciousness.

00:09:01.039 --> 00:09:03.837
You must find me very odd, Kes.

00:09:03.875 --> 00:09:05.900
No, of course not.
Try to keep still.

00:09:08.379 --> 00:09:11.075
So... what should I call you?

00:09:11.115 --> 00:09:13.083
Ah, a name.

00:09:13.117 --> 00:09:14.914
I hadn't thought of that.

00:09:14.953 --> 00:09:16.921
What an intriguing question.

00:09:16.955 --> 00:09:18.752
I can see why the Doctor

00:09:18.790 --> 00:09:21.588
is finding it
so difficult to choose one.

00:09:21.626 --> 00:09:24.254
A name can have
a significant effect

00:09:24.295 --> 00:09:26.786
upon a person's
sense of identity.

00:09:27.832 --> 00:09:29.925
I've got it.

00:09:29.968 --> 00:09:31.333
What?

00:09:32.971 --> 00:09:34.939
Why don't you call me...

00:09:34.973 --> 00:09:36.406
Neevok.

00:09:37.408 --> 00:09:38.932
Wait.

00:09:40.845 --> 00:09:43.814
This is better.

00:09:43.848 --> 00:09:45.941
How about Tuvix?

00:09:45.984 --> 00:09:48.179
Tuvix it is.

00:09:48.219 --> 00:09:52.588
I'm so glad you're here to help
me through this, sweeting.

00:09:54.092 --> 00:09:56.060
I'm sorry.

00:09:56.094 --> 00:09:58.460
It was instinct.

00:10:01.266 --> 00:10:03.962
Why don't we finish the scan.

00:10:12.243 --> 00:10:14.643
Chief Medical Officer's Log,
supplemental.

00:10:14.679 --> 00:10:17.307
Extensive microcellular scans
on the merged humanoid

00:10:17.348 --> 00:10:19.680
have, thus far, yielded
no clues to either a cause

00:10:19.717 --> 00:10:22.550
or a method of separation.

00:10:22.587 --> 00:10:24.885
Ah, Captain, so good
of you to come.

00:10:24.922 --> 00:10:26.219
How are you feeling?

00:10:26.257 --> 00:10:27.519
I feel well.

00:10:27.558 --> 00:10:29.992
You might even say...

00:10:30.061 --> 00:10:31.460
exhilarated.

00:10:31.496 --> 00:10:32.861
I'm glad to hear it.

00:10:32.897 --> 00:10:35.127
Well, that's what I wanted
to talk to you about.

00:10:35.166 --> 00:10:36.292
In the past 24 hours,

00:10:36.334 --> 00:10:38.564
I've undergone
rigorous diagnostic testing,

00:10:38.603 --> 00:10:39.934
submitted to an extensive

00:10:39.971 --> 00:10:41.438
psychological profile

00:10:41.472 --> 00:10:43.599
and I've been poked and prodded

00:10:43.641 --> 00:10:46.474
in organs that I
didn't even know I had.

00:10:46.511 --> 00:10:51.744
While all this testing
may no doubt be necessary...

00:10:51.783 --> 00:10:53.683
frankly, I'm restless.

00:10:53.718 --> 00:10:55.185
To tell you the truth,

00:10:55.219 --> 00:10:58.120
we could use a little help
in the Mess Hall.

00:10:58.156 --> 00:11:00.351
And I'd be glad
to give you a hand.

00:11:00.391 --> 00:11:02.291
But...

00:11:02.327 --> 00:11:03.851
after careful consideration,

00:11:03.895 --> 00:11:07.160
I've decided that the most
sensible thing for me to do

00:11:07.198 --> 00:11:09.063
is to resume the tactical post.

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:10.067
Tactical?

00:11:10.101 --> 00:11:11.966
Remember, Captain,

00:11:12.003 --> 00:11:14.528
I do possess Tuvok's
knowledge and expertise,

00:11:14.572 --> 00:11:16.199
and while I have no doubt

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:19.971
that the crew misses
Neelix's cooking,

00:11:20.044 --> 00:11:23.536
you need your most
experienced Tactical Officer.

00:11:23.581 --> 00:11:25.549
That's me.

00:11:27.085 --> 00:11:28.143
If I may, Captain.

00:11:28.186 --> 00:11:29.153
Mr. Tuvix...

00:11:29.187 --> 00:11:30.381
Tuvix?

00:11:30.421 --> 00:11:32.889
Apparently, that's what
he likes to be called.

00:11:32.924 --> 00:11:35.893
Mr. Tuvix is, indeed,
in perfect health.

00:11:35.927 --> 00:11:37.827
And since I've collected
all the data I need,

00:11:37.862 --> 00:11:39.659
there's no reason I can't
continue my investigation

00:11:39.697 --> 00:11:41.528
without him for the time being.

00:11:41.566 --> 00:11:43.329
And, according to my tests,
he's quite correct

00:11:43.368 --> 00:11:46.428
when he says that he possesses
Tuvok's knowledge and expertise.

00:11:46.471 --> 00:11:47.938
He also possesses

00:11:47.972 --> 00:11:50.440
Tuvok's irritating sense
of intellectual superiority

00:11:50.475 --> 00:11:54.912
and Neelix's
annoying ebullience.

00:11:54.946 --> 00:11:56.675
I would be very grateful to you

00:11:56.714 --> 00:11:58.739
if you would assign him
some duty.

00:12:01.085 --> 00:12:02.109
Any duty...

00:12:02.153 --> 00:12:05.020
somewhere else.

00:12:07.058 --> 00:12:10.653
Well... Mr. Tuvix...

00:12:10.695 --> 00:12:13.528
I'm not ready to assign you
to the Bridge just yet,

00:12:13.564 --> 00:12:15.794
but why don't you
join the senior staff

00:12:15.833 --> 00:12:16.959
for our noon briefing,

00:12:17.068 --> 00:12:19.195
and we'll see
how it goes from there.

00:12:19.237 --> 00:12:22.263
Captain, has anyone
ever told you

00:12:22.306 --> 00:12:25.867
that you are as fair-minded
as you are lovely?

00:12:25.910 --> 00:12:27.571
As a matter of fact,

00:12:27.612 --> 00:12:30.706
Neelix has told me that
occasionally.

00:12:30.748 --> 00:12:33.979
And if you really do
possess his memories...

00:12:34.085 --> 00:12:37.953
you'd know that flattery
will get you nowhere.

00:12:40.658 --> 00:12:42.853
The transporter
was functioning normally.

00:12:42.894 --> 00:12:45.692
Biofilters, pattern buffers,
everything checked out.

00:12:45.730 --> 00:12:46.992
What about the problem

00:12:47.031 --> 00:12:48.999
with the molecular
imaging scanners?

00:12:49.033 --> 00:12:50.500
According
to the transporter logs,

00:12:50.535 --> 00:12:52.435
they were optimal
at the time of transport.

00:12:52.470 --> 00:12:54.995
It was a perfectly routine
beam-out sequence.

00:12:55.072 --> 00:12:58.974
No anomalies, no power
overloads, no malfunctions.

00:12:59.010 --> 00:13:00.910
Our scans of the planet's
surface and atmosphere

00:13:00.945 --> 00:13:03.209
don't show anything
out of the ordinary.

00:13:03.247 --> 00:13:06.375
There's no evidence of any type
of alien interference.

00:13:06.417 --> 00:13:08.282
Frankly, Captain,
we're at a loss.

00:13:08.319 --> 00:13:09.946
And the orchids, Kes?

00:13:10.054 --> 00:13:12.488
Have you found anything
unusual about them?

00:13:12.523 --> 00:13:15.424
Commander Chakotay brought back
a few samples on the shuttle

00:13:15.460 --> 00:13:17.257
and I ran
a biochemical analysis.

00:13:17.295 --> 00:13:20.598
They contain the same elements
as many plants: Chloroplasts,

00:13:20.731 --> 00:13:23.222
lysosomal enzymes,
cytoplasmic proteins,

00:13:23.267 --> 00:13:25.201
but there's nothing unusual.

00:13:25.235 --> 00:13:27.169
There's never been an accident
like this recorded

00:13:27.204 --> 00:13:29.297
in the entire history
of transporter technology.

00:13:29.340 --> 00:13:32.138
I'm not willing to accept it
as a random malfunction.

00:13:32.176 --> 00:13:34.644
Captain, I recommend we program
a holodeck simulation,

00:13:34.678 --> 00:13:36.270
try recreating the accident.

00:13:36.313 --> 00:13:38.304
Sex.

00:13:39.583 --> 00:13:40.914
I beg your pardon?

00:13:40.951 --> 00:13:42.714
What I mean to say is...

00:13:42.753 --> 00:13:45.813
and I apologize
for cutting you off, Commander...

00:13:45.856 --> 00:13:48.086
I think
we're on the wrong track.

00:13:48.125 --> 00:13:52.494
Kes... you said that the flowers
you examined

00:13:52.529 --> 00:13:54.326
contained lysosomal enzymes.

00:13:54.365 --> 00:13:55.423
That's right.

00:13:55.466 --> 00:13:57.832
According to Tuvok's
botanical research,

00:13:57.868 --> 00:13:59.859
the presence
of lysosomal enzymes

00:13:59.903 --> 00:14:03.168
could be evidence
of symbiogenesis.

00:14:03.207 --> 00:14:04.697
Symbiogenesis?

00:14:04.742 --> 00:14:08.644
Symbiogenesis is a rare
reproductive process.

00:14:08.679 --> 00:14:10.510
Instead of pollination
or mating,

00:14:10.547 --> 00:14:13.778
symbiogenetic organisms merge
with a second species.

00:14:13.817 --> 00:14:15.682
Andorian amoebae, for instance...

00:14:15.719 --> 00:14:19.849
they're able to merge with
other single-celled organisms

00:14:19.890 --> 00:14:21.949
to form a third unique species.

00:14:22.059 --> 00:14:23.424
A hybrid.

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:24.722
Like you.

00:14:24.762 --> 00:14:27.060
Exactly.

00:14:27.097 --> 00:14:28.496
It's an interesting idea,

00:14:28.532 --> 00:14:31.296
but we're talking about
microcellular organisms here.

00:14:31.335 --> 00:14:33.565
I've never heard
of symbiogenesis occurring

00:14:33.604 --> 00:14:35.629
in a species as complex
as a humanoid.

00:14:35.673 --> 00:14:37.971
Actually, Captain,
when you think about it,

00:14:38.075 --> 00:14:39.940
Neelix and Tuvok
were broken down

00:14:39.977 --> 00:14:43.743
to a microcellular level
during transport... DNA,

00:14:43.781 --> 00:14:47.683
protein, all in a state
of molecular flux.

00:14:47.718 --> 00:14:51.711
And if the enzymes
that cause symbiogenesis

00:14:51.755 --> 00:14:53.245
interacted with their DNA

00:14:53.290 --> 00:14:54.518
while they were
in the matter stream,

00:14:54.558 --> 00:14:57.186
it might've caused
their patterns to merge.

00:14:57.227 --> 00:14:58.990
Like an Andorian amoeba.

00:14:59.029 --> 00:15:02.487
Just like that, Tuvix is born.

00:15:04.168 --> 00:15:06.728
It's the best theory
I've heard so far.

00:15:06.770 --> 00:15:08.601
It's the only theory
I've heard so far.

00:15:08.639 --> 00:15:10.436
And it's worth investigating.

00:15:10.474 --> 00:15:12.203
Mr. Paris, take a shuttle
to the planet

00:15:12.242 --> 00:15:14.039
and collect additional
flower specimens.

00:15:14.078 --> 00:15:17.172
Yes, ma'am, but I'd recommend
waiting until morning.

00:15:17.214 --> 00:15:18.579
The weather on the planet
can get

00:15:18.615 --> 00:15:19.775
pretty nasty at night.

00:15:19.817 --> 00:15:22.285
Very well.
You'll depart at 600 hours.

00:15:28.225 --> 00:15:30.386
Good work, Mr. Tuvix.

00:15:45.075 --> 00:15:46.542
Kes.

00:15:46.577 --> 00:15:48.511
Oh, hello.

00:15:48.545 --> 00:15:50.604
Hello.

00:15:50.647 --> 00:15:53.172
Do you need something?

00:15:53.217 --> 00:15:55.412
Actually, I was wondering

00:15:55.452 --> 00:15:57.977
if you'd like
to join me for dinner.

00:15:58.055 --> 00:16:00.148
Well, I, uh...

00:16:00.190 --> 00:16:01.122
You've already eaten?

00:16:01.158 --> 00:16:02.887
Well, no.

00:16:02.926 --> 00:16:03.858
You're not hungry?

00:16:03.894 --> 00:16:04.861
Actually...

00:16:04.895 --> 00:16:06.886
If memory serves me,

00:16:06.930 --> 00:16:08.921
Wednesday's the day

00:16:09.032 --> 00:16:11.432
that Neelix always cooked
Trellan crepes...

00:16:11.468 --> 00:16:13.663
your favorite meal?

00:16:13.704 --> 00:16:14.762
That's right.

00:16:14.805 --> 00:16:16.932
Well, why break with tradition

00:16:17.040 --> 00:16:20.168
just because of a little
transporter accident?

00:16:23.781 --> 00:16:25.078
Somebody's eggs are burning!

00:16:25.115 --> 00:16:26.082
Those are mine.

00:16:26.116 --> 00:16:27.640
Can you flip them for me?

00:16:27.684 --> 00:16:29.208
I can't find a spatula.

00:16:29.253 --> 00:16:31.847
Just... try tossing them.

00:16:31.889 --> 00:16:33.356
Why don't you have a seat?

00:16:33.390 --> 00:16:35.449
I'll be with you in a minute.

00:16:35.492 --> 00:16:38.518
Do you mind telling me
what's going on here, crewman?

00:16:38.562 --> 00:16:40.553
We're making dinner.

00:16:42.399 --> 00:16:44.367
I see.

00:16:44.401 --> 00:16:46.528
All right, everybody out!

00:16:46.570 --> 00:16:47.696
On whose authority?

00:16:47.738 --> 00:16:50.229
Chief of Security or Head Chef...

00:16:50.274 --> 00:16:51.332
take your pick.
Out, out, out!

00:16:52.442 --> 00:16:53.409
Come, come.

00:16:53.443 --> 00:16:55.434
Out!

00:17:07.658 --> 00:17:09.421
So you really enjoyed
the crepes?

00:17:09.459 --> 00:17:11.086
Oh, they were
absolutely delicious.

00:17:11.128 --> 00:17:12.322
Don't you think Neelix

00:17:12.362 --> 00:17:13.795
always made them
a little too spicy?

00:17:13.831 --> 00:17:15.560
These were a little
different than usual.

00:17:15.599 --> 00:17:17.032
Did you change the recipe?

00:17:17.067 --> 00:17:18.091
Only slightly.

00:17:18.135 --> 00:17:20.228
I thought more moderate
seasoning would allow

00:17:20.270 --> 00:17:22.363
the flavor of the mushrooms
to come through.

00:17:22.406 --> 00:17:23.668
I loved the mushrooms.

00:17:23.707 --> 00:17:25.174
I'm glad.

00:17:25.209 --> 00:17:26.176
I can't believe

00:17:26.210 --> 00:17:27.939
how disorganized
this galley was.

00:17:28.011 --> 00:17:30.343
It's a wonder Neelix
ever found anything.

00:17:30.380 --> 00:17:32.507
He says he has a system.

00:17:32.549 --> 00:17:34.983
But I guess
you already know that.

00:17:36.220 --> 00:17:38.518
I admire your strength, Kes.

00:17:38.555 --> 00:17:40.216
Why do you say that?

00:17:40.257 --> 00:17:41.690
I know I'm not Neelix,

00:17:41.725 --> 00:17:44.193
but I can posit
with complete certainty

00:17:44.228 --> 00:17:46.355
that if the situation
were reversed...

00:17:46.396 --> 00:17:49.957
if suddenly he found himself
without you in his life...

00:17:50.067 --> 00:17:52.501
he'd be absolutely lost.

00:17:57.608 --> 00:17:59.974
I have to go.

00:18:00.010 --> 00:18:02.274
Thanks again for dinner.

00:18:13.956 --> 00:18:15.651
Good morning, Captain.
Commander.

00:18:15.691 --> 00:18:17.318
You're here bright and early,
Lieutenant.

00:18:17.359 --> 00:18:19.054
Actually, I've been here
since 0400 hours.

00:18:19.094 --> 00:18:21.824
I wanted to work on that
proximity detector glitch

00:18:21.863 --> 00:18:23.296
in the security subroutine.

00:18:23.332 --> 00:18:24.390
And how's it going?

00:18:24.433 --> 00:18:26.401
I managed to correct it.

00:18:26.435 --> 00:18:28.096
Tuvok said it could
take up to ten days

00:18:28.136 --> 00:18:29.933
to check out all
the possible problems.

00:18:29.972 --> 00:18:31.064
How'd you fix it so fast?

00:18:31.106 --> 00:18:32.164
I had a hunch.

00:18:32.207 --> 00:18:33.174
"A hunch"?

00:18:33.208 --> 00:18:34.607
That's correct.

00:18:34.643 --> 00:18:36.167
You'll have a report
on your desk

00:18:36.211 --> 00:18:37.906
first thing this afternoon.

00:18:37.946 --> 00:18:39.106
Kim to Mr. Tuvix.

00:18:39.147 --> 00:18:40.546
Tuvix here.

00:18:40.582 --> 00:18:41.742
We're just about ready

00:18:41.783 --> 00:18:43.683
to start the transporter tests,
if you'd like to join us.

00:18:43.719 --> 00:18:44.879
I'm on my way.

00:18:44.920 --> 00:18:46.319
Excuse me, Captain.

00:18:50.959 --> 00:18:53.689
Well, he's certainly
fitting in, isn't he?

00:18:53.729 --> 00:18:55.162
There's an old axiom:

00:18:55.197 --> 00:18:58.189
"The whole is never greater
than the sum of its parts."

00:18:58.233 --> 00:19:01.293
I think Tuvix might be
disproving that notion.

00:19:11.146 --> 00:19:13.910
Give me the flowers
from the airponics bay.

00:19:13.982 --> 00:19:15.847
Here you go.

00:19:15.884 --> 00:19:18.478
One prize-winning
chrysanthemum...

00:19:20.655 --> 00:19:23.590
one garden-variety clematis...

00:19:25.994 --> 00:19:28.656
and last but not least...

00:19:33.435 --> 00:19:36.370
one symbiogenetic alien orchid.

00:19:40.409 --> 00:19:42.377
I never thought
that botanical science class

00:19:42.411 --> 00:19:43.605
would come in so handy.

00:19:49.418 --> 00:19:51.386
Torres to Transporter Room 1.

00:19:51.420 --> 00:19:52.648
We're ready down here.

00:19:52.687 --> 00:19:54.018
Acknowledged.

00:19:55.690 --> 00:19:57.157
Energizing.

00:20:10.005 --> 00:20:13.168
We've made over 100 attempts
to reverse the symbiogenesis

00:20:13.208 --> 00:20:14.903
using the medical transporter,

00:20:14.943 --> 00:20:18.071
and each time, this has been
the unfortunate result...

00:20:18.113 --> 00:20:20.206
complete cellular collapse.

00:20:20.248 --> 00:20:22.375
The genetic codes
of the chrysanthemum

00:20:22.417 --> 00:20:24.385
and the clematis
are so scrambled

00:20:24.419 --> 00:20:25.886
that the targeting scanners

00:20:25.921 --> 00:20:27.889
can't recognize
the original patterns.

00:20:27.923 --> 00:20:30.619
I suppose it would be
like trying to extract

00:20:30.659 --> 00:20:34.095
the flour, eggs and water
after you'd baked the cake.

00:20:34.129 --> 00:20:35.926
Obviously,
in the case of Mr. Tuvix,

00:20:35.964 --> 00:20:38.990
we're dealing with a much more
complex organism than a flower.

00:20:39.101 --> 00:20:40.363
In effect, we're talking

00:20:40.402 --> 00:20:42.370
about recreating
two humanoid life-forms

00:20:42.404 --> 00:20:44.565
without so much
as a single discrete strand

00:20:44.606 --> 00:20:45.903
of DNA to start with.

00:20:45.941 --> 00:20:48.637
Are you saying I'm going
to be this way forever?

00:20:49.644 --> 00:20:51.305
I am an incredibly
skilled doctor

00:20:51.346 --> 00:20:53.007
and I will continue to pursue

00:20:53.081 --> 00:20:56.209
a safe and effective
treatment until I find one...

00:20:56.251 --> 00:20:57.878
but I won't lie to you.

00:20:57.919 --> 00:20:59.318
I'm not optimistic.

00:20:59.354 --> 00:21:02.448
It could take months, even
years, to find a solution.

00:21:02.491 --> 00:21:06.154
And we must face the possibility
that this condition is simply...

00:21:06.194 --> 00:21:08.219
untreatable.

00:21:08.263 --> 00:21:11.960
I feel as though
I've lost two patients.

00:21:12.033 --> 00:21:13.261
I'm sorry.

00:21:17.272 --> 00:21:19.604
I'll inform the rest
of the crew.

00:21:40.328 --> 00:21:41.625
Come in.

00:21:43.565 --> 00:21:45.465
I hope I'm not disturbing you.

00:21:45.500 --> 00:21:47.331
It's all right.

00:21:48.837 --> 00:21:50.964
Um, please...

00:21:51.006 --> 00:21:52.371
sit down.

00:21:52.407 --> 00:21:55.103
Ocampan prayer tapers.

00:21:55.143 --> 00:21:56.633
For Tuvok and Neelix?

00:21:58.346 --> 00:21:59.472
It's funny...

00:21:59.514 --> 00:22:03.143
if something happened to Tuvok,
if Neelix were here,

00:22:03.185 --> 00:22:05.653
he'd be the first person
to comfort me.

00:22:05.687 --> 00:22:07.951
And if I lost Neelix...

00:22:08.023 --> 00:22:12.187
Tuvok would be the first person
to guide me spiritually.

00:22:13.862 --> 00:22:16.194
Now I don't have either of them.

00:22:16.231 --> 00:22:18.756
You have me, Kes.

00:22:18.800 --> 00:22:21.667
Thank you.

00:22:21.703 --> 00:22:22.931
But...

00:22:22.971 --> 00:22:25.804
I remind you
of what you've lost.

00:22:25.840 --> 00:22:27.501
It's not your fault.

00:22:27.542 --> 00:22:32.445
I know, and I'm trying
to accept who I am now.

00:22:32.480 --> 00:22:33.845
Captain Janeway tells me

00:22:33.882 --> 00:22:36.350
there's a place
for me on this ship...

00:22:36.384 --> 00:22:40.411
but I can't help feeling like...

00:22:40.455 --> 00:22:42.889
like some sort of impostor.

00:22:42.924 --> 00:22:45.825
Maybe we can help
each other get through this.

00:22:45.860 --> 00:22:48.124
That's what I've been hoping.

00:22:50.732 --> 00:22:53.792
I know this is going to sound
very strange to you...

00:22:53.835 --> 00:22:55.962
perhaps even illogical...

00:22:56.004 --> 00:23:00.998
since, in a way, we've only
known each other a few days.

00:23:01.076 --> 00:23:03.943
But I want you to know...

00:23:04.012 --> 00:23:05.775
I love you, Kes.

00:23:05.814 --> 00:23:08.282
But I hardly know you.

00:23:10.285 --> 00:23:13.812
A-And besides, what about...

00:23:13.855 --> 00:23:16.688
what about Tuvok's wife,
for one thing?

00:23:16.725 --> 00:23:18.488
He was completely
devoted to her.

00:23:18.526 --> 00:23:20.960
What happens when Voyager
gets back home?

00:23:20.996 --> 00:23:22.896
Are you just going
to forget her?

00:23:22.931 --> 00:23:24.956
I could never forget T'Pel.

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:27.628
I carry Tuvok's love
for her inside me

00:23:27.669 --> 00:23:30.502
and I would never ask you
to forget Neelix.

00:23:30.538 --> 00:23:32.972
How can you talk this way?

00:23:33.041 --> 00:23:39.674
Because I carry Neelix's love
for you inside me, as well,

00:23:39.714 --> 00:23:41.409
and I always will.

00:23:41.449 --> 00:23:43.280
You heard the Doctor.

00:23:43.318 --> 00:23:44.717
It could be years

00:23:44.753 --> 00:23:47.688
before he finds a way to bring
Tuvok and Neelix back...

00:23:47.722 --> 00:23:49.952
if ever.

00:23:49.991 --> 00:23:54.018
For you,
that might be a lifetime.

00:23:59.334 --> 00:24:00.824
Please go.

00:24:00.869 --> 00:24:02.302
I'm sorry.

00:24:02.337 --> 00:24:06.296
I should've controlled
my emotions.

00:24:06.341 --> 00:24:09.504
All I really came to say

00:24:09.544 --> 00:24:13.503
is that I'll be here for you
if you need me.

00:24:42.143 --> 00:24:43.110
Kes.

00:24:43.144 --> 00:24:44.304
Captain.

00:24:44.346 --> 00:24:45.973
I'm sorry. I shouldn't
have bothered you this late.

00:24:46.081 --> 00:24:47.548
I'll, uh, talk to you tomorrow.

00:24:47.582 --> 00:24:49.982
Actually, I was having
trouble sleeping.

00:24:50.018 --> 00:24:51.576
I could use some company.

00:24:53.521 --> 00:24:55.182
Would you like some hot tea?

00:24:55.223 --> 00:24:56.713
Please, sit down.

00:24:59.294 --> 00:25:01.929
I was just looking over
some old letters Tuvok sent me

00:25:02.062 --> 00:25:04.622
when he was temporarily
assigned to Jupiter Station.

00:25:04.665 --> 00:25:06.428
Most people would say

00:25:06.466 --> 00:25:11.335
his writing is cold,
analytical, detached, but...

00:25:11.371 --> 00:25:14.340
I've always found it to be...

00:25:14.374 --> 00:25:16.399
concise, efficient...

00:25:18.645 --> 00:25:20.840
...thoughtful.

00:25:20.881 --> 00:25:25.944
I hear his voice
when I read the words.

00:25:26.053 --> 00:25:28.146
And Neelix...

00:25:29.923 --> 00:25:32.050
I'd become so fond of him, Kes.

00:25:32.092 --> 00:25:34.959
I can't imagine
what you're going through.

00:25:34.995 --> 00:25:37.429
I wanted to talk
to you about Tuvix.

00:25:37.464 --> 00:25:39.694
He came to see me
this afternoon.

00:25:39.733 --> 00:25:40.825
Oh?

00:25:40.867 --> 00:25:44.769
He said... he said
that he loves me.

00:25:48.075 --> 00:25:50.839
I suppose I can see
how that's possible,

00:25:50.877 --> 00:25:52.310
given the circumstances.

00:25:52.346 --> 00:25:54.439
I wasn't sure what to say.

00:25:54.481 --> 00:25:56.346
At first I was angry,

00:25:56.383 --> 00:26:00.149
but I know how he's
trying to comfort me

00:26:00.187 --> 00:26:02.621
and I know that he feels alone,
too.

00:26:02.656 --> 00:26:06.490
To tell the truth,
he's a wonderful person.

00:26:06.526 --> 00:26:09.188
Do you have feelings
for him, too, Kes?

00:26:09.229 --> 00:26:10.457
No, I don't.

00:26:11.798 --> 00:26:13.322
I mean, how could I?

00:26:13.367 --> 00:26:16.063
I still love Neelix...

00:26:16.103 --> 00:26:18.594
and I'm not ready
to give up on him,

00:26:18.638 --> 00:26:20.936
no matter what the Doctor says.

00:26:21.008 --> 00:26:25.945
I know how you feel.

00:26:26.046 --> 00:26:27.206
You're experiencing

00:26:27.247 --> 00:26:29.306
what people on this crew
have been going through

00:26:29.349 --> 00:26:32.147
since we first got stranded
in this Quadrant.

00:26:33.487 --> 00:26:34.784
Do we accept

00:26:34.821 --> 00:26:38.348
that we're separated
from our loved ones forever?

00:26:38.392 --> 00:26:40.121
Or do we hold on to the hope

00:26:40.160 --> 00:26:42.924
that, someday,
we'll be with them again?

00:26:45.499 --> 00:26:47.091
What do you do, Captain?

00:26:48.902 --> 00:26:51.393
Oh... I struggle with it
every day.

00:26:51.438 --> 00:26:53.929
Sometimes, I'm full
of hope and optimism.

00:26:55.675 --> 00:26:58.007
Other times...

00:27:00.580 --> 00:27:02.946
I dream about being with Mark...

00:27:05.852 --> 00:27:07.444
...and it's so real.

00:27:10.590 --> 00:27:14.924
Then, when I wake up
and realize it's just a dream,

00:27:15.028 --> 00:27:17.087
I'm terribly discouraged.

00:27:19.099 --> 00:27:20.464
In those moments,

00:27:20.500 --> 00:27:24.937
it's impossible to deny
just how far away he really is.

00:27:25.038 --> 00:27:27.336
And, uh...

00:27:31.111 --> 00:27:35.343
I know that, someday,

00:27:35.382 --> 00:27:40.843
I may have to accept that he's
not part of my life anymore.

00:27:40.887 --> 00:27:43.788
So, are you saying
that I should just accept

00:27:43.824 --> 00:27:46.622
that Neelix isn't a part
of my life anymore?

00:27:46.660 --> 00:27:49.527
I would never tell you
or anyone else

00:27:49.563 --> 00:27:51.360
to give up hope, Kes.

00:27:53.200 --> 00:27:55.930
I think the best thing
you can do now...

00:27:55.969 --> 00:27:58.460
is give yourself time.

00:28:00.207 --> 00:28:01.902
Thank you, Captain.

00:28:04.878 --> 00:28:08.507
I'll go now and let you sleep.

00:28:11.017 --> 00:28:14.384
My door is always open to you,
Kes.

00:28:31.404 --> 00:28:35.363
Captain's Log, Stardate 49678.4.

00:28:35.408 --> 00:28:37.103
It's been two weeks

00:28:37.144 --> 00:28:40.375
since the transporter accident
that created Mr. Tuvix

00:28:40.413 --> 00:28:42.244
and, while it's still
not entirely clear

00:28:42.282 --> 00:28:43.840
that he's with us permanently,

00:28:43.884 --> 00:28:47.149
he's certainly been doing
his best to settle in.

00:28:47.187 --> 00:28:50.054
The crew seems to be growing
accustomed to his presence,

00:28:50.090 --> 00:28:52.684
and he's proving to be
a very able Tactical Officer

00:28:52.726 --> 00:28:55.092
who isn't afraid
to express his opinions.

00:28:55.128 --> 00:28:58.894
While he's forging relationships
with many of the officers,

00:28:58.932 --> 00:29:02.333
he seems to be keeping a
respectful distance from Kes,

00:29:02.369 --> 00:29:04.599
allowing her to adjust
to the circumstances

00:29:04.638 --> 00:29:06.503
on her own terms.

00:29:06.540 --> 00:29:09.771
As for my relationship
with Tuvix,

00:29:09.809 --> 00:29:11.777
I've found him
to be an able advisor,

00:29:11.811 --> 00:29:14.575
who skillfully uses humor
to make his points.

00:29:14.614 --> 00:29:18.482
And although I feel
a bit guilty saying it,

00:29:18.518 --> 00:29:21.180
his cooking is better
than Neelix's.

00:29:21.221 --> 00:29:24.486
My taste buds are definitely
happy to have him around.

00:29:45.845 --> 00:29:47.506
Sick Bay to Ensign Kim.

00:29:47.547 --> 00:29:50.209
Please turn to your emergency
medical holographic channel.

00:29:58.191 --> 00:29:59.453
How can I help you, Doc?

00:29:59.492 --> 00:30:00.959
Suppose I found a radioisotope

00:30:01.061 --> 00:30:03.393
that could selectively
attach itself

00:30:03.430 --> 00:30:05.091
to specific DNA sequences.

00:30:05.131 --> 00:30:06.962
Could the surgical transporters
be reprogrammed

00:30:07.067 --> 00:30:09.126
to lock on
to those enhanced sequences

00:30:09.169 --> 00:30:11.967
and separate them
from the remaining DNA?

00:30:12.005 --> 00:30:14.064
Well, I think so,

00:30:14.107 --> 00:30:16.701
but we'd have to modify
the molecular imaging scanners,

00:30:16.743 --> 00:30:20.235
and find a way to compensate for
the higher levels of radiation.

00:30:20.280 --> 00:30:21.542
Thank you, Ensign.

00:30:21.581 --> 00:30:22.980
Wait a second.

00:30:23.049 --> 00:30:25.711
What's going on?

00:30:25.752 --> 00:30:27.583
It's pure speculation
at this point.

00:30:27.621 --> 00:30:29.748
I'll let you know
when I've learned more.

00:30:29.789 --> 00:30:32.189
This is about Tuvix, isn't it?

00:30:32.225 --> 00:30:33.453
I'm on my way.

00:30:45.005 --> 00:30:47.098
Eight ball, corner pocket.

00:30:56.449 --> 00:30:58.144
That's game again, Commander.

00:30:58.184 --> 00:31:00.448
We've created a monster.

00:31:00.487 --> 00:31:02.421
Best out of five?

00:31:15.068 --> 00:31:17.536
Would you mind if we finished
this later, Commander?

00:31:17.570 --> 00:31:18.662
Not at all.

00:31:25.979 --> 00:31:27.207
Hi.

00:31:27.247 --> 00:31:28.373
Hi.

00:31:33.820 --> 00:31:35.481
How have you been?

00:31:35.522 --> 00:31:37.990
Good days and bad days.

00:31:38.024 --> 00:31:38.991
You?

00:31:39.025 --> 00:31:40.117
Me, too.

00:31:40.160 --> 00:31:42.526
Listen, I'm sorry I've been
so distant lately.

00:31:42.562 --> 00:31:46.430
Kes, you don't owe me
an explanation.

00:31:47.667 --> 00:31:49.430
I've been doing
a lot of thinking.

00:31:52.272 --> 00:31:54.706
And I'm hoping
that we can be friends.

00:31:57.410 --> 00:32:01.904
I would like that very much.

00:32:01.948 --> 00:32:03.939
And I'd like our friendship
to grow.

00:32:04.050 --> 00:32:05.608
You would?

00:32:05.652 --> 00:32:07.142
Yes.

00:32:07.187 --> 00:32:09.212
But it's going to take time.

00:32:12.292 --> 00:32:14.783
I'm not going anywhere.

00:32:16.963 --> 00:32:19.227
Doctor to Lieutenant Tuvix.

00:32:21.201 --> 00:32:22.964
Tuvix here.

00:32:23.036 --> 00:32:25.004
Please report
to Sick Bay immediately.

00:32:27.440 --> 00:32:30.432
Until late in the 21st century,

00:32:30.477 --> 00:32:32.411
physicians administered
barium to patients

00:32:32.445 --> 00:32:34.310
with certain
gastrointestinal disorders.

00:32:34.347 --> 00:32:36.178
The radioactive properties
of the barium

00:32:36.216 --> 00:32:37.808
made the lining
of the intestines visible,

00:32:37.851 --> 00:32:40.513
with a primitive imaging
technology called X rays.

00:32:40.553 --> 00:32:44.455
Instead of barium, we've
come up with a radioisotope

00:32:44.491 --> 00:32:45.458
that attaches itself

00:32:45.492 --> 00:32:47.187
to the DNA of one
of the merged species,

00:32:47.227 --> 00:32:49.422
but not the other.

00:32:49.462 --> 00:32:51.760
Then we simply beam out
the selected DNA,

00:32:51.798 --> 00:32:54.426
and segregate
the two merged species.

00:32:58.037 --> 00:32:59.868
You see these?

00:32:59.906 --> 00:33:03.171
They used to be
a single merged flower.

00:33:03.209 --> 00:33:04.608
And you can use
this same process?

00:33:04.644 --> 00:33:05.770
It will require

00:33:05.812 --> 00:33:08.110
a more detailed reprogramming
of the transporter,

00:33:08.148 --> 00:33:10.878
but, yes, I believe
we can restore

00:33:10.917 --> 00:33:13.715
Mr. Tuvok and Mr. Neelix.

00:33:13.753 --> 00:33:15.550
That's wonderful.

00:33:15.588 --> 00:33:16.885
Isn't that wonderful?

00:33:18.191 --> 00:33:20.955
I assure you, Mr. Tuvix,
there's nothing to worry about.

00:33:20.994 --> 00:33:22.859
We've accounted
for every variable.

00:33:24.597 --> 00:33:26.360
Except one.

00:33:27.600 --> 00:33:30.091
I don't want to die.

00:33:39.811 --> 00:33:41.176
It's funny...

00:33:41.212 --> 00:33:44.579
if we'd had the ability
to separate Tuvok and Neelix

00:33:44.615 --> 00:33:46.606
the moment Tuvix came aboard...

00:33:46.651 --> 00:33:48.278
I wouldn't have hesitated.

00:33:48.319 --> 00:33:49.877
Of course not.

00:33:49.921 --> 00:33:51.320
But now...

00:33:51.356 --> 00:33:53.324
in the past few weeks...

00:33:53.358 --> 00:33:57.317
he's begun to make a life
for himself on this ship.

00:33:57.362 --> 00:33:59.296
He's taken on
responsibilities...

00:33:59.330 --> 00:34:00.524
made friends...

00:34:00.565 --> 00:34:03.329
I count myself as one of them.

00:34:03.368 --> 00:34:06.496
So, at what point did
he become an individual

00:34:06.537 --> 00:34:08.732
and not a transporter accident?

00:34:13.711 --> 00:34:14.700
Come in.

00:34:16.314 --> 00:34:18.248
You wanted to see me, Captain?

00:34:20.385 --> 00:34:21.875
Yes, Mr. Tuvix.

00:34:21.919 --> 00:34:23.580
Please, sit down.

00:34:27.458 --> 00:34:28.857
I feel as though

00:34:28.893 --> 00:34:31.953
I've been dragged in front
of the Numirian Inquisition.

00:34:31.996 --> 00:34:34.863
Will you excuse us, Commander?

00:34:39.437 --> 00:34:42.838
We've just been discussing
the unfortunate...

00:34:42.874 --> 00:34:46.708
predicament
that we're all facing,

00:34:46.744 --> 00:34:50.475
and I thought it was important
to get your perspective

00:34:50.515 --> 00:34:52.813
before making a decision.

00:34:52.850 --> 00:34:56.547
Are you suggesting that this
is your decision to make?

00:34:56.587 --> 00:34:58.953
I am the Captain of this ship.

00:34:58.990 --> 00:35:01.151
Begging your pardon, Captain,

00:35:01.192 --> 00:35:02.591
it's my life.

00:35:02.627 --> 00:35:04.219
Isn't it my decision?

00:35:04.262 --> 00:35:07.493
Aren't there two other lives
to consider here?

00:35:07.532 --> 00:35:09.796
What about Tuvok and Neelix...

00:35:09.834 --> 00:35:13.497
two voices that we
can't hear right now?

00:35:13.538 --> 00:35:16.803
As Captain,
I must be their voice,

00:35:16.841 --> 00:35:19.639
and I believe
they would want to live.

00:35:19.677 --> 00:35:21.611
But they are living, in a way.

00:35:21.646 --> 00:35:22.806
Inside me.

00:35:22.847 --> 00:35:25.145
It's not the same.

00:35:25.183 --> 00:35:27.583
And I think you'd agree with me.

00:35:30.221 --> 00:35:32.086
They have families.

00:35:32.123 --> 00:35:33.385
Friends.

00:35:33.424 --> 00:35:35.187
People who love them

00:35:35.226 --> 00:35:37.854
and miss them
and want them back,

00:35:37.895 --> 00:35:39.328
just as I do.

00:35:39.363 --> 00:35:43.766
But restoring their lives
means sacrificing mine.

00:35:43.801 --> 00:35:45.063
Captain...

00:35:45.102 --> 00:35:48.469
what you're considering
is an execution.

00:35:48.506 --> 00:35:50.201
An execution...

00:35:50.241 --> 00:35:53.210
like they used to do
to murderers centuries ago...

00:35:53.244 --> 00:35:55.576
and I've committed
no crime at all.

00:35:55.613 --> 00:35:58.673
Aren't you arguing
for an execution, too...

00:35:58.716 --> 00:36:00.650
of Tuvok and Neelix?

00:36:00.685 --> 00:36:03.313
I'm here... alive.

00:36:03.354 --> 00:36:06.323
Unfortunate as it may be,
they're gone.

00:36:06.357 --> 00:36:08.848
And I have an opportunity
to bring them back.

00:36:08.893 --> 00:36:13.330
Don't you think that I care
about Tuvok and Neelix?

00:36:13.364 --> 00:36:14.922
Of course I do!

00:36:14.999 --> 00:36:17.433
Without them, I wouldn't exist.

00:36:17.468 --> 00:36:20.232
In a way, I think of them
as my parents.

00:36:20.271 --> 00:36:22.739
I feel like
I know them intimately.

00:36:22.773 --> 00:36:24.934
Then you know Tuvok was a man

00:36:25.042 --> 00:36:28.341
who would gladly give
his life to save another.

00:36:28.379 --> 00:36:31.371
And I believe the same
was true of Neelix.

00:36:32.984 --> 00:36:34.747
You're right, Captain.

00:36:36.754 --> 00:36:39.052
That is the Starfleet way.

00:36:40.391 --> 00:36:42.757
And I know there'll be
some people

00:36:42.793 --> 00:36:44.624
who will call me a coward

00:36:44.662 --> 00:36:48.462
because I didn't
sacrifice myself willingly.

00:36:48.499 --> 00:36:52.230
Believe me,
I've thought of that.

00:36:52.270 --> 00:36:55.967
But I have the will to live
of two men.

00:36:56.073 --> 00:36:59.975
Look at me, Captain.

00:37:00.077 --> 00:37:03.478
When I'm happy, I laugh.

00:37:03.514 --> 00:37:05.209
When I'm sad, I cry.

00:37:05.249 --> 00:37:09.743
When I stub my toe,
I yell out in pain.

00:37:09.787 --> 00:37:12.153
I'm flesh and blood.

00:37:12.189 --> 00:37:17.092
And I... have the right
to live!

00:37:35.413 --> 00:37:36.710
Kes...

00:37:38.215 --> 00:37:40.683
I need your help.

00:37:40.718 --> 00:37:42.777
I've just come from the Captain,

00:37:42.820 --> 00:37:45.118
and she's thinking
about forcing me

00:37:45.156 --> 00:37:47.590
to go through
with the separation.

00:37:49.393 --> 00:37:52.794
If anybody can make
a difference, Kes, it's you.

00:37:52.830 --> 00:37:54.730
She'll listen to you.

00:37:54.765 --> 00:37:56.960
We've helped each other
through this,

00:37:57.034 --> 00:38:02.472
and I know that you care
about what happens to me.

00:38:02.506 --> 00:38:04.474
Please.

00:38:04.508 --> 00:38:07.033
Kes, you may be my only hope.

00:38:15.720 --> 00:38:17.415
Come in.

00:38:19.757 --> 00:38:21.281
Captain...

00:38:21.325 --> 00:38:24.522
Tuvix has asked me
to speak to you on his behalf.

00:38:28.399 --> 00:38:31.095
But I can't.

00:38:31.135 --> 00:38:33.330
He shouldn't have put you
in the middle of this.

00:38:33.371 --> 00:38:35.032
But I am in the middle.

00:38:35.072 --> 00:38:38.064
I have been since
the moment of the accident.

00:38:39.543 --> 00:38:42.774
I don't know how to say good-bye
to Neelix and Tuvok.

00:38:45.650 --> 00:38:48.210
I know this sounds horrible...

00:38:48.252 --> 00:38:51.244
and I feel so guilty
for saying it...

00:38:53.324 --> 00:38:56.816
and Tuvix doesn't
deserve to die...

00:38:58.162 --> 00:39:01.495
but I want Neelix back.

00:39:17.081 --> 00:39:19.072
You're excused, Ensign.

00:39:24.889 --> 00:39:27.449
Mr. Paris,
what is our present speed?

00:39:27.491 --> 00:39:29.891
Warp 6.5.

00:39:29.927 --> 00:39:33.920
I'd like to conduct a field test
of the aft sensor array.

00:39:34.031 --> 00:39:36.329
Please, slow to impulse.

00:39:38.269 --> 00:39:39.531
Commander?

00:39:39.570 --> 00:39:42.403
Until the Captain
makes a decision,

00:39:42.440 --> 00:39:45.773
Mr. Tuvix is still
the Tactical Officer.

00:40:12.136 --> 00:40:13.535
Mr. Tuvix?

00:40:14.905 --> 00:40:16.964
I'd like to speak to you alone.

00:40:17.074 --> 00:40:19.736
Can I assume that you've
come to a decision, Captain?

00:40:21.345 --> 00:40:22.972
I have.

00:40:23.080 --> 00:40:26.811
I think we all should hear
what you have to say!

00:40:28.385 --> 00:40:30.410
Please come with me, Mr. Tuvix.

00:40:32.423 --> 00:40:33.617
No.

00:40:34.792 --> 00:40:38.592
I'm ordering you
to come with me.

00:40:43.099 --> 00:40:44.828
Security to the Bridge.

00:40:44.867 --> 00:40:47.665
Commander, are you going
to stand by and do nothing

00:40:47.703 --> 00:40:49.500
while she commits murder?!

00:40:51.307 --> 00:40:52.331
Wha?

00:40:52.375 --> 00:40:53.706
Mr. Ayala!

00:40:55.544 --> 00:40:56.841
Yes...

00:40:56.879 --> 00:40:59.177
Lieutenant Paris...

00:40:59.215 --> 00:41:00.375
you...

00:41:03.552 --> 00:41:06.851
Doesn't anyone see
that this is wrong?!

00:41:27.076 --> 00:41:29.408
Let him go.

00:41:33.716 --> 00:41:39.052
Each of you is going to have
to live with this...

00:41:40.423 --> 00:41:42.983
and I'm sorry for that.

00:41:43.092 --> 00:41:47.256
For you are all good...
good people.

00:41:48.764 --> 00:41:50.493
My colleagues.

00:41:53.502 --> 00:41:55.060
My friends.

00:41:59.375 --> 00:42:01.843
I forgive you.

00:42:14.790 --> 00:42:16.382
Commander Chakotay,

00:42:16.425 --> 00:42:19.451
advise the Doctor
we're on our way to Sick Bay.

00:42:22.731 --> 00:42:24.289
Deck 5.

00:42:42.751 --> 00:42:44.651
I'm sorry, Captain,

00:42:44.687 --> 00:42:47.588
but I cannot perform
the surgical separation.

00:42:47.623 --> 00:42:52.617
I am a physician,
and a physician must do no harm.

00:42:52.661 --> 00:42:56.222
I will not take Mr. Tuvix' life
against his will.

00:42:56.265 --> 00:42:58.961
Very well, Doctor.

00:42:59.001 --> 00:43:01.128
Please step aside.

00:43:10.045 --> 00:43:13.014
I assume this is
the radioisotope.

00:43:15.551 --> 00:43:17.883
Please sit down on this bio-bed.

00:43:49.418 --> 00:43:51.648
Locking surgical
targeting scanners

00:43:51.687 --> 00:43:54.815
onto the isotope probe.

00:43:54.857 --> 00:43:58.020
Initiating separation sequence.

00:44:06.535 --> 00:44:08.332
Energizing.

00:44:24.420 --> 00:44:25.546
Neelix!

00:44:25.588 --> 00:44:27.852
Hello, sweeting!

00:44:29.592 --> 00:44:31.321
Greetings, Captain.

00:44:31.360 --> 00:44:33.954
Mr. Tuvok...

00:44:34.063 --> 00:44:36.531
Mr. Neelix...

00:44:36.565 --> 00:44:38.726
it's good to have you back.
